    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT1G20050-MONOMER" textLabel="AT1G20050-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O48962" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="475" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">NIL The C-8,7 sterol isomerase catalyzes the conversion of 4&amp;alpha;-methylfecosterol to 24-methylenelophenol in the higher plant sterol biosynthetic pathway by removal of a hydrogen from the 7&amp;beta; position and the subsequent addition of a hydrogen at the 9&amp;alpha; position , reducing the existing &amp;Delta;&lt;sup&gt;8(9)&lt;/sup&gt; double bond and producing the &amp;Delta;&lt;sup&gt;7(8)&lt;/sup&gt; double bond of the sterol B ring. The &lt;i&gt;HYD1&lt;/i&gt; cDNA encoding a C-8,7 sterol isomerase was isolated from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt;. When expressed in a &lt;i&gt;&amp;Delta;erg2&lt;/i&gt; yeast strain deficient in C-8,7 sterol isomerase, &lt;i&gt;HYD1&lt;/i&gt; complemented the mutant phenotype |CITS:[9862498]|. Epistatic studies of sterol biosynthesis mutant in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; confirmed that HYD1 substrate is 4&amp;alpha;-methylfecosterol |CITS:[12034894][12100483][15078327]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G20050-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G20050.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR14207" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Arrayexpress" value="O48962" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_String" value="O48962" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pride" value="O48962" />
